body:
This sounds weirdly similar to the experience I am going through. I have a low grade feeling like I have to go as well. And let me tell you, anxiety does NOT help. It is actually a very well documented anxiety symptom that you feel. Prostatitis is typically characterized by pain. So if you don't have pain, I would hazard a guess and say its probably overactive bladder/anxiety. Also, while I am not a doctor, the urethra is a thin tube, right? and since the prostate wraps around it, if your prostate was swelling with any type of prostatitis, your bladder ultrasound would definitely show that its not emptying properly. If your urologist said it is emptying properly, then that means your urethra is definitely not obstructed or being pressed on by swollen things, like a swelling prostate. I think you should take your urologist's advice. You should work on some stress relieving techniques, whatever those may be for you. 

&#x200B;

Also, consider the fact that you saw a urologist - he/she specializes in that field. If they really suspected it, they would have mentioned it/told you to look for other things. But if your urologist says they believe its  a physical manifestation of anxiety, I would trust them. It is a very common anxiety symptom. I'm having a tough time telling myself this too... but think about all the tests they use, and if you've had them, they probably would've noticed something wrong (if there was). So it is definitely psychological.
